    { "id": "biblical", "title": "Biblical vs Modern Hebrew", "body": [
      "Same alphabet, roots and most core words: yom, láyla, or, máyim, érets, tov, ki. You can already read much of Genesis 1.",
      "Differences: Biblical prose usually puts the **verb first** (bará elohím: created God); it marks definite objects with **et** (Modern does too); it has no **shel** (it uses construct chains); and it tells stories with the **vav-consecutive** (next lesson).",
      "Pronunciation: Israelis read the Bible with Modern pronunciation; scholarly reconstructions differ (pharyngeal ḥ, ʕ like Arabic)."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ", "tr": "bereshít bará elohím et ha-shamáyim ve-ét ha-árets", "en": "In the beginning God created the heavens and the earth" }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "bb1", "prompt": "Biblical word for 'in the beginning':", "answer": "בְּרֵאשִׁית", "tr": "bereshít" },
      { "id": "bb2", "prompt": "What does אֵת mark?", "answer": "אֵת", "tr": "et: the definite direct object" },
      { "id": "bb3", "prompt": "Say: Let there be light.", "answer": "יְהִי אוֹר", "tr": "yehí or" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "vav", "title": "The vav-consecutive: וַיֹּאמֶר", "concept": "aspect", "body": [
      "Biblical narrative uses **va-** + the *future* form to mean the *past*: **va-yómer** = and he said (Modern: ve-hu amár); **va-yár** = and he saw; **va-yehí** = and there was.",
      "Spot it by the **וַ** with a dagesh in the next letter: וַיֹּאמֶר, וַיַּרְא. Once you know it, most Biblical stories open up."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַיְהִי אוֹר", "tr": "va-yómer elohím yehí or va-yehí or", "en": "And God said, let there be light, and there was light" }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "vv1", "prompt": "Biblical 'and he said':", "answer": "וַיֹּאמֶר", "tr": "va-yómer" },
      { "id": "vv2", "prompt": "Biblical 'and he saw':", "answer": "וַיַּרְא", "tr": "va-yár" },
      { "id": "vv3", "prompt": "Modern Hebrew for וַיֹּאמֶר:", "answer": "וְהוּא אָמַר", "tr": "ve-hú amár" }
    ], "verified": false }
